 all localized actions. MR is R⊗_Z M, and iota is the balanced multiplication map from LinearMap.liftBaseChange. Jcoord is the inverse image of its range under c↦c e_i; rationalMu is multiplication Q⊗_R J→C. coordinateFacts gives the exact direct-sum isomorphism with its sum formula, rationalFacts includes finite dimensionality as well as finrank=1 and injectivity, and principalFacts supplies the scalar b and actual localized basis. Module.finrank is Cardinal.toNat of rank: it is used as dimension only with the explicit finite basis or finite-dimensional conditions.\nUse the standard scalar-first tensor convention VK=K⊗_Z M throughout. The source writes M⊗_Z K; the canonical symmetry sends c⊗m to m⊗c, identifies K scalar multiplication on the first factor with that on the second, and identifies f.baseChange K with the source action on pure tensors. This is an order convention for one representation, not a second independent model. T008 explicitly constructs the source's substantive scalar-extension and reduction bridges, in this convention. ModN(MR,p) is the quotient by the range of integer multiplication by p, which is exactly pMR, with its canonical ZMod p module. The existential ring homomorphisms bar and eps supply the actual R and prime-field scalar actions on K; they are conclusions, never premise instances. Pure-tensor forward and inverse formulas and intertwining obligations fix the meanings of both bridges.\nIntegralOps contains only integer-linear restrictions with equality to the complex operators after inclusion; existence is proved in T003. Their components are unique by injectivity of inclusion of M, so all compatible bundles induce the same operators on VK. This avoids any definition choosing restrictions before their existence is proved. reductionFacts quantifies over every compatible bundle and supplies the basis, matrix units, nonzero binomials and factorial power identities. Invariant subspaces are actual Submodule K objects; stable means closure 